---
alwaysApply: true
---
1. Code Style & Formatting

Use Prettier defaults: 2 spaces, semicolons, single quotes, and trailing commas.

Keep line length under 100 characters where possible.

Organize imports in this order: external libraries → internal modules → styles.

Remove unused imports and variables.

2. React & JSX

Always use functional components with hooks — never class components.

Type all props using TypeScript interfaces.

Prefer explicit typing and avoid any.

Use controlled components for form inputs.

Break down large JSX into smaller reusable components.

3. State Management

Use @bigcommerce/checkout-sdk for accessing and updating checkout state.

Use React hooks like useState, useEffect, useMemo, and useCallback.

Avoid deep prop drilling — use context providers when necessary.

4. Error Handling

Always handle async code with try/catch or .catch().

Show errors through UI components such as ErrorModal or ErrorBoundary.

Do not use console.error for production errors, only for debugging.

5. Commits & PRs

Follow Conventional Commits (feat:, fix:, chore:).

Keep pull requests small, focused, and well-documented.

Write clear commit messages that explain the “why,” not just the “what.”

8. General Practices

Prefer composition over inheritance.

Write self-documenting code; only use comments for complex logic.

Always consider accessibility (use aria-labels, roles, and ensure keyboard navigation).
